    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div>I&#39;ve had to go back in time an eternity but, after taking a look, I think ˋextractEFAparameters()ˋ was originally not intended to be called directly. That&#39;s what the message is saying, that it is not a fucntion that is available for you to call. Originally, this was only called from within ˋreadModels()ˋ. Does the latter solve your problem?</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">For what I can see ˋextractEFAparameters()ˋ is now documented, so it should be exported. This is clearly a bug to be solved.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\" dir=\"auto\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
