     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I tried to make a quick fix, would you be so kind as to try it <a class=\"gmail_plusreply\" href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">@Catia Oliveira</a> ?</div><div><br></div><div>Please run the following:</div><div><br></div><div>if (!require(&quot;devtools&quot;)) install.packages(&quot;devtools&quot;)</div><div>devtools::install_github(&quot;DaniMori/MplusAutomation@bugfix/export-efa-params&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>And then run your code again. Please let me know if it works then.<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El vie, 8 mar 2024 a las 15:40, Daniel Morillo Cuadrado (&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danivm...@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\"><div>I&#39;ve had to go back in time an eternity but, after taking a look, I think ˋextractEFAparameters()ˋ was originally not intended to be called directly. That&#39;s what the message is saying, that it is not a fucntion that is available for you to call. Originally, this was only called from within ˋreadModels()ˋ. Does the latter solve your problem?</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">For what I can see ˋextractEFAparameters()ˋ is now documented, so it should be exported. This is clearly a bug to be solved.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\" dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El vie, 8 mar 2024, 15:07, &#39;Catia Oliveira&#39; via MplusAutomation &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>mplusau...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<div><br></div><div>I hope you are well.</div><div>I tried to use &quot;extractEFAparameters&quot; to read the parameters from EFA into R but it did not work:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><i><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"># Load the MplusAutomation package</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;whit