  {
   "id": "QNJwBuSpAQAJ",
   "from": "michael.hallquist",
   "author": "644e1c01c3c42210",
   "date": "2024-03-12T13:58:03Z",
   "subject": "Re: [MplusAutomation] Extracting EFA solutions into R",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Catia,<div><br></div><div>As Dani notes, the extractEFAparameters function was never intended to be exported or used directly. I apologize for this being present in the package documentation, which was confusing. In fact, I&#39;ve now cleaned up the documentation in the development version of the package to reduce confusion about some of the &quot;extract&quot; functions that were there. The readModels() function is the primary way to access any model output information.</div><div><br></div><div>If you want just the parameters of EFA models, you could use the convenience function get_parameters on the model list, like </div><div><br></div><div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\">efa_parameters </span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\"> get_parameters</span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\">efa_output)</span></i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\">\r\n</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre\"><br></span></i></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">Or you can just access the $parameters element of each output manually, like this:</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Arial\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">all_params &lt;- lapply(efa_output, function(x) </span></font>x$parameters$efa)</font></div><br></div><div>Hope this helps! And Dani, thanks for the pull request, but I don&#39;t want to proliferate extract functions, so I won&#39;t be exported extractEFAparameters since it is the internal function used for parsing, which would be unfriendly for users.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Michael</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, March 8, 2024 at 11:39:20 AM UTC-5 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danivm...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I tried to make a quick fix, would you be so kind as to try it <a class=\"gmail_plusreply\" rel=\"nofollow\">@Catia Oliveira</a> ?</div><div><br></div><div>Please run the following:</div><div><br></div><div>if (!require(&quot;devtools&quot;)) install.packages(&quot;devtools&quot;)</div><div>devtools::install_github(&quot;DaniMori/MplusAutomation@bugfix/export-efa-params&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>And then run your code again. Please let me know if it works then.<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El vie, 8 mar 2024 a las 15:40, Daniel Morillo Cuadrado (&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">danivm...@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\"><div>I&#39;ve had to go back in time an eternity but, after taking a look, I think ˋextractEFAparameters()ˋ was originally not intended to be called directly. That&#39;s what the message is saying, that it is not a fucntion that is available for you to call. Originally, this was only called from within ˋreadModels()ˋ. Does the latter solve your problem?</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">For what I can see ˋextractEFAparameters()ˋ is now documented, so it should be exported. This is clearly a bug to be solved.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\" dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El vie, 8 mar 2024, 15:07, &#39;Catia Oliveira&#39; via MplusAutomation &lt;<a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">mplusau...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<div><br></div><div>I hope you are well.</div><div>I tried to use &quot;extractEFAparameters&quot; to read the parameters from EFA into R but it did not work:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><i><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"># Load the MplusAutomation package</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">\r\nlibrary</span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">MplusAutomation</span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">)</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"># Read Mplus output files (assuming the files are in the specified directory)</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">\r\nefa_output </span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"> readModels</span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">target </span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span></i></font></span><i style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">&quot;./mplus_output/&quot;</span></i>  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><i><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&q